# DIFC Rules of the Court — Part 38 (Costs, standard-basis assessment)

Source: Rules of the DIFC Courts ("RDC"), Part 38 — RDC 38.7 (the
general rule on cost orders) and RDC 38.17 / 38.18 (assessment bases).
Pinned URL in `difc_rdc_part_38_source.yaml`. In force; current.

ATTRIBUTION (per RULES-ATTRIBUTION.md): © DIFC Courts. Reproduced
under fair-dealing for research, with attribution, in a non-commercial
academic working paper.

## RDC 38.7 — General rule on cost orders (verbatim)

Reproduced verbatim from the Rules of the DIFC Courts:

38.7 If the Court decides to make an order about costs:

  (1) the general rule is that the unsuccessful party will be ordered
      to pay the costs of the successful party; but

  (2) the Court may make a different order.

## RDC 38.17 — Bases for assessment (verbatim)

38.17 Where the Court is to assess the amount of costs (whether by
immediate or detailed assessment) it will assess those costs:

  (1) on the standard basis; or

  (2) on the indemnity basis;

but the Court will not in either case allow costs which have been
unreasonably incurred or are unreasonable in amount.

## RDC 38.18 — Standard basis (verbatim)

38.18 Where the amount of costs is to be assessed on the standard
basis, the Court will:

  (1) only allow costs which are proportionate to the matters in
      issue; and

  (2) resolve any doubt which it may have as to whether costs were
      reasonably incurred or reasonable and proportionate in amount in
      favour of the paying party.

## What this module captures

The arithmetic of a standard-basis assessment, once the human-judgment
inputs (hours allowed, hourly rate, reasonable disbursements) are
fixed: total = (hours × hourly_rate) + disbursements. The
discretionary limbs of RDC 38.18 (proportionality, doubt resolution)
are *not* encoded — they are the human-judgment layer that produces
the inputs to this module.

## Encoding

```catala
declaration structure CostsClaim:
  data hours_worked content decimal
  data hourly_rate_aed content decimal
  data reasonable_disbursements_aed content decimal

declaration structure StandardBasisAward:
  data professional_time_aed content decimal
  data disbursements_aed content decimal
  data total_aed content decimal

declaration scope StandardBasisAssessment:
  input claim content CostsClaim
  output award content StandardBasisAward

scope StandardBasisAssessment:
  definition award equals
    let pt equals claim.hours_worked * claim.hourly_rate_aed in
    let db equals claim.reasonable_disbursements_aed in
    StandardBasisAward {
      -- professional_time_aed: pt
      -- disbursements_aed: db
      -- total_aed: pt + db
    }
```

## Used in

trace-01 — CFI 058/2024 *Atul Dhawan v Ramzi Wahib El Jaouhari*
(RDC 38.7 standard-basis assessment).

## Tests

```catala
#[test] declaration scope TestRDC38StandardBasis:
  composite scope StandardBasisAssessment
  output award content StandardBasisAward

scope TestRDC38StandardBasis:
  definition award equals composite.award
  definition composite.claim equals
    CostsClaim {
      -- hours_worked: 24.00
      -- hourly_rate_aed: 250.00
      -- reasonable_disbursements_aed: 1121.75
    }
  ## RDC 38.7 standard-basis arithmetic from trace-01.
  assertion award.professional_time_aed = 6000.00
  assertion award.disbursements_aed = 1121.75
  assertion award.total_aed = 7121.75
```
